  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Avatar seats, no matter how small the seat is, can be accessed from far distances. Ive often had people accidentally click on it when they werent even facing me. Can we have a range slider or option for how close you have to be to click on the chair in Unity? Some chairs you want to make as accessable as possible so they'd leave it on the far range, but for those of us with (for example)  \"backpack\" chairs that we dont mind being on all the time, we'd like to make them only close range clickable so we dont grab anyone by accident.",
